## Verdict: ★ REGISTER CLIFF REACHED (v31 -> v30) = HOLDS side (min-fold lever engages despite the qh plane)
# - maxVreg v31 -> v30 at BOTH -O2 and -O3: the <=32-vreg register cliff WAS REACHED — the SAME
#   v31->v30 step q4_K S6 and q2_K T3 hit. q6_K T3 and q3_K T3 (dual-plane / no-min weight-bound)
#   NEVER left v31. So by the campaign's mechanistic discriminator, q5_K is on the HOLDS side:
#   the shared kquant_dmin_bsums_min min-fold register-cliff lever TRANSFERS to q5_K and SURVIVES
#   the qh 5th-bit weight plane.
# - vwmacc 2240 UNCHANGED across all four => byte-exact MAC multiset preserved (confirmed by the
#   IDENTITY-DUMP o_untiled.bin == o_tiled.bin, 0 mismatch, and both oracle verifies PASS 8.0e-07).
# - reload (vl*r.v) 288 -> 110 (-62%): the S6 scale/min int16 + i32 bsums stack-panels cut hot-loop
#   reload traffic by nearly two-thirds — this is the throughput lever (register-resident hot dot).
# - spill (vs*r.v) 155 -> 105 (-32%): DROPPED but did NOT collapse to ~0 (contrast q2_K 619->7,
#   q4_K 84->3). This is the QH PLANE FOOTPRINT: q5_K carries a 5th-bit weight-reconstruction plane
#   (qh, the SHARED weight_qh_byte_offset slot, here on the MIN fold) that the decode-scale/min panel
#   does NOT stage — so a ~105-spill residual floor remains. q5_K's UNTILED spill was already only
#   155 (NOT the 600-900 of q2_K/q6_K), because untiled q5_K was already lean and already a ~1.55x
#   WIN vs the opponent block-dot (unlike q2_K's 619-spill 0.21x LOSS regime). So there was less
#   absolute spill to collapse; the decisive move is the peak-vreg drop below 32 + the -62% reload cut.
# - textB ~flat (37774 -> 38506, +2%; NOT halved like q2_K 51014->26968): the hot dot stays fully
#   unrolled (4480 src vwmacc both forms) and the panel store/load bands add a little code; the win is
#   register-residency + peak-vreg-below-cliff, not code shrink.

## Hot-loop spill classification (TILED -O2): first 20 vs*r.v addresses
#   The early 0xbc/0xd4/0xe2/0x106/0x120 + 0x22e/0x244/0x258/0x26e cluster are prologue whole-register
#   saves (function-boundary, benign). From 0x54a onward the recurring `vs1r.v v19,(a0)` at a regular
#   ~0x8a stride are the per-h-strip qh-plane / weight-materialization spills that the min-fold panel
#   does not cover — the residual weight-bound floor. (Full disassembly on the board scratch, ephemeral.)
