## The transfer boundary (q5_K places on the map)
# q4_K / q2_K  (pure kquant_dmin_bsums_min min-fold): v31->v30, spill->~0, HUGE win        = HOLDS (full collapse)
# q5_K         (min-fold + qh 5th-bit weight plane):  v31->v30, spill 155->105, +42% win   = HOLDS (min-fold lever
#              reaches the cliff; qh plane leaves a residual spill floor — a HYBRID, not the full collapse)
# q6_K / q3_K  (dual-plane / no-min weight-bound):     v31->v31, spill ~flat, NULL          = NULL (weight-bound)
# => q5_K confirms the min-fold register-cliff lever DOMINATES enough to cross the <=32 cliff even WITH
#    a weight plane present. The qh plane is a SECONDARY residual (105 floor), not the dominant pressure.
